¥lines‘‚¤textÙQSeest thou how faith wrought with his works, and by works was faith made perfect?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–And the scripture was fulfilled which saith, Abraham believed God, and it was imputed unto him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHYe see then how that by works a man is justified, and not by faith only.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒLikewise also was not Rahab the harlot justified by works, when she had received the messengers, and had sent them out another way?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPFor as the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without works is dead also.¦layout ªlast_verse